<%# @spec QUESTION-EXPLORATION-015
    The Inbox page keeps `py-8` below the stacked and split detail panes, so
    its embedded panel must reserve that same 2rem of viewport space at every
    breakpoint. The chat controller measures the panel's actual document
    offset after this frame is installed; together these keep the conversation
    scrollable and composer reachable without the full chat-page shell. At
    `lg`+ the panel's `--chat-panel-height` resolves to `100%` (set by the
    `[data-controller~="chat"]` rule) so it stays bounded to the shared
    `list-detail` grid track and the inner `lg:overflow-y-auto` wrapper does
    not become a second scroll container in front of the transcript (#4374
    review). The Inbox host page gives the `<turbo-frame id="inbox-detail">`
    matching the `frame_id` local `block h-full` so the panel's `height:
    100%` can resolve against the shared grid track through the otherwise
    `display: inline` (content-height) turbo-frame element. %>
<%= turbo_frame_tag frame_id do %>
  <%= turbo_stream_from current_account, :chat_sessions %>
  <%= turbo_stream_from chat_session.project, :chat_sessions if chat_session.project_scoped_exploration? %>
  <%= render "chat_sessions/chat_panel",
             chat_session: chat_session,
             chat_messages: chat_messages,
             has_older_messages: has_older_messages,
             can_update_chat_session: can_update_chat_session,
             can_archive_chat_session: can_archive_chat_session,
             can_unarchive_chat_session: can_unarchive_chat_session,
             available_runners: available_runners,
             available_models: available_models,
             chat_panel_bottom_space: "2rem" %>
<% end %>
